F05 session 29 - identifier identity + surface corroboration (2026-11-15)
=========================================================================
Mechanism fixes (no example-specific rules):
1. lib/web-search/normalization.ts now owns ONE identity layer:
   identityShapes(text, join) / foldIdentityToken / identityForms /
   wordIdentityForms / splitCoreWords. A "+"/"#" modifier run is part of the
   identifier (C++ -> c++, C# -> c#, F# -> f#); alternate spellings come only
   from the neutral separators . _ - and the apostrophe (next.js <-> nextjs,
   O'Brien <-> obrien retained). Query side and text side share the code.
2. metasearch.ts: mentionTokenSet -> wordIdentityForms, normalizeToken ->
   foldIdentityToken, countLexicallyRelevant -> foldIdentityToken.
   reranker.ts tokenize -> identityShapes(text, "none").
   Effect: a "C" page can no longer be reported as mentioning "C++" (or the
   reverse) and the BM25 reranker no longer loses symbol identifiers.
3. presentation.ts: NEW corroborateSurface(plan, userPrompt, evidenceDomains)
   applied inside derivePresentation() only. A finance/sports/tracker surface
   selected by TWO ambiguous words must be corroborated by a vertical evidence
   domain, unless the prompt matches that rung PRIMARY pattern. Nothing can
   add a surface; it can only decline an unsupported one (same shape as the
   pre-existing news rule). planPresentation() and every reason string / field
   order stay byte-identical, so all pinned positives survive.

NOT REPRODUCED (recorded with evidence, per reproduce-before-changing):
- case-sensitivity of rust/zig/nim deciding support: no such logic exists
  (git grep of zig/nim under lib/ returns none); both sides lowercase.
- reranker substring relevance: scoring is token-set based; the only includes()
  uses are domain checks.
- cache-key incompleteness: queryCacheKey already hashes
  query|freshness|intent|domains|anchor|gl; pageCacheKey carries ab=/bw=
  fingerprints.
- locale-as-identity: local-context.ts explicitRegionCc + query-planner
  linkedinSearchHosts already treat machine locale as a fallback hint only.
  The explicit-Italy -> in.linkedin.com gap is real but collides with the
  pinned given-name ambiguity law; left scoped and documented.
- ALIAS limitation recorded: c++ does not match cpp; shapes are not aliases.

